    "q-35273": {
      "dom_id": "step-q35273",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "If \n$F=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]$, find $\\text{rank}(F).$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the rank of $F,$ we first reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 14 & 13 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+7{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $3$ non-zero rows).\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(F)=3.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
