    "q-79559": {
      "dom_id": "step-q79559",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Which of the following matrices has a rank of $5?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that a matrix of rank $5$ must have at least $5$ columns and at least $5$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the following matrices:\n\n- $B$ since it has only $2$ rows.\n\n- $C$ since it has only $3$ columns.\n\n- $D$ since it has only $3$ rows (and only $3$ columns).\n\nAlso, the matrix must have $5$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $A$ has exactly $5$ pivot columns, while the matrix $E$ has only $4$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(A)=5$ and $\\text{rank}(E)=4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the matrix $A.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-79559-a",
